<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<component name="JRPoster" extends="Poster">
  <children>
    <RectangleSecondary id="watchBadgeBackground" width="90" height="48" visible="false">
      <LabelPrimarySmall id="unplayedVideosCount" isBold="true" height="48" horizAlign="center" vertAlign="center" translation="[0,3]" />
      <LabelPrimaryMedium id="checkmark" isBold="true" height="48" horizAlign="center" vertAlign="center" text="✓" translation="[0,3]" visible="false" />
    </RectangleSecondary>
    <!--
      Placement, and what is NOT yet decided about it.

      This badge sits bottom-left, clear of the progress bar's strip, and the watched/unplayed
      badge keeps top-right. That much is deliberate: top-right has held the watched badge since
      long before this and jellyfin-web puts its unplayed count there too, and versions belongs by
      the progress bar because both answer "what happens if I press Play".

      What is NOT settled is the badge SYSTEM — whether further signals get their own corners or
      join a single rail, and which metadata earns a tile at all. jellyfin-web lays every card
      indicator out in ONE top-right flex rail of round chips (`.cardIndicators`) and shows no
      HDR / Dolby Vision / Atmos / resolution on cards at all; JellyRock already diverges in chip
      shape and size. With only two badges today the question is not forced, and measured tile
      widths (213 and 264 px portrait) say a rail of three 48 px chips would take 75% of the
      narrow poster, so it is not a free choice either. Settle it BEFORE adding a third badge —
      see `poster-badge-system-undesigned` in docs/architecture/tech-debt.md.

      Two things that ARE load-bearing whatever gets decided:
        * every badge must be cleared in resetBadge() — these cells are recycled, and an
          uncleared badge ghosts onto the next item;
        * this badge is drawn on a colorBlack+alpha60 scrim rather than the accent colour,
          because VideoProgressBar fills its bar with colorSecondary and an accent chip directly
          above it merged into a single blue block on a partly-watched tile (caught on device).
    -->
    <Rectangle id="versionsBadgeBackground" width="48" height="48" visible="false">
      <Poster id="versionsIcon" uri="pkg:/images/icons/layers_$$RES$$.png" width="40" height="40" translation="[4,4]" />
    </Rectangle>
  </children>
  <interface>
    <field id="unplayedCount" type="integer" value="0" />
    <field id="isWatched" type="boolean" value="false" />
    <field id="playedPercentage" type="float" value="0" />
    <field id="mediaSourceCount" type="integer" value="0" />
    <function name="resetBadge" />
  </interface>
</component>